{
  "$comment": "A run executed on the web reads the same on the desktop, and the other way round (EJE-06). Both sides start from `project` and `cases` (pulled documents, revision 1), create `run` with `items` and record `attempts`; what each side then stores, normalized (`normalize`), must equal `documents`. Then each side applies `documents` as pulled documents and its run screen must equal `views` (normalized the same way). Read by src-tauri/src/runs/web_vectors_tests.rs and server/tests/runs.test.ts. `normalize`: ids made by each side are replaced by the names here, in creation order (the run by `run`, items by position, step results by `<result id>:<position>`); the listed bookkeeping keys (clock, author, local workspace and times written at save) become \"*\". The third case is a legacy one (plain-text steps, written by an older client) with a custom field: both sides derive the same step ids for it. `pulledOnly` is an imported run (shard and result, linked by its tag) that only the desktop writes: both sides read it the same in `views.importedResults`.",
